# A module function's bare `ctr is 99` where `ctr` is not a top-level binding
# of the module — ouroboros#141 arm B (the issue's first comment).
#
# THE POINT OF THIS FIXTURE is that renaming a module's TOP-LEVEL bindings —
# the fix the issue body specified — is not sufficient. `is` is outward-
# mutable, so after splicing, a bare `ctr is 99` inside a module function
# writes the MERGED scope, i.e. the program's `ctr`:
#
#   VM   99 / 1          AOT (top-level rename only)   99 / 99, rc 0, empty log
#
# On the VM the module's search stops at its boundary (EigenScript#1056 /
# #373): a name the module never bound at its top level is a FRESH binding in
# the module's own namespace, never the importer's. So the rename set must
# cover every free assignment target at any depth (`collect_free_assigns`),
# not just `module_bindings`. Deleting that line is the planted fault this
# fixture is gated on — it goes red as 99/99.
ctr is 1
import _arm_mz
print of (_arm_mz.bump of null)
print of ctr
